                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "229284014",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198315886368",
                            "num_reviews": 251,
                            "playtime_forever": 142,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 120,
                            "last_played": 1792616825
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Honestly, this game just infuriates me. I'm at the second world and I already find the whole thing tedious and annoying. There's 200 levels and about nothing interesting for most of them. Most of the time you're just dealing with depth perception and enemies just come across as a nuisance. Power-ups are far and few between and there's nothing that keeps me from being invested in this game. Doesn't help that the music, while decent, is repetitive since you're dealing with 4 worlds with 50 levels each. Make it 8 worlds with 25 levels and that would be more tolerable with more world variation. There's also a speed run timer but the game offers no replay value with doing this and is just overall boring. At least the gameplay is very polished but seriously, I'd spend my money elsewhere.",
